WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.420
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:18.720
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:34.720
Go Fish: collect four of a rank
Players receive hands and the remaining cards form the stock. Follow Demo N through three hands, collecting four matching ranks into books.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:46.820
Choose rank and player, then Ask
Click a hand card to choose its rank, click an opponent with cards, then press Ask. You may choose in either order or cancel and reselect.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:56.720
Ask only for a rank in your own hand. You cannot ask yourself or an empty-handed player.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:07.720
Receive every matching card and ask again
Follow public asks and turn changes. A target holding that rank gives every matching card, and the asker continues.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:16.720
Asks and transfer counts are public; unrelated hand cards remain hidden.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:27.720
Four matching ranks form a book
Watch the next book entry. Collecting all four cards of one rank automatically removes them from the hand and adds one book.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:36.722
No four-card selection or separate Book button is needed. Public asks can help you choose a target later.

00:01:36.722 --> 00:01:56.722
Speed through to your first book
Repeated asks run faster until your own book appears in the log. The controls remain rank, player, then Ask.

00:01:56.722 --> 00:02:09.922
A failed ask fishes automatically
If the target lacks that rank, the game draws one card automatically. Matching the asked rank keeps your turn; otherwise the turn passes.

00:02:09.922 --> 00:02:20.721
An unmatched draw stays hidden from others. An empty hand automatically receives a card while stock remains.

00:02:20.721 --> 00:02:40.721
Complete all thirteen books
Speed through the first hand’s final asks, books, and refills. Once all 13 books are complete, scores accumulate and the next hand is dealt.

00:02:40.721 --> 00:03:14.721
Speed through all three hands
All asks, fishing draws, books, and refills in hands two and three play in order at higher speed. An empty stock can still leave asks to resolve.

00:03:14.721 --> 00:03:33.734
Go Fish: cumulative book totals
Demo E wins with 13 books. Demo S has 12, N has 11, and W has 3.
